# This is a whitelist, not the usual blacklist: everything is ignored, and only
# our own source files are allowed back in.
#
# Why: the build directory sits inside a Crysis 2 installation, so Crytek files
# (SDK headers, import libraries generated from retail DLLs, cursor resources
# extracted from Crysis2.exe) live right next to ours. A normal blacklist would
# let any newly added file slip into a commit unnoticed. Here nothing reaches
# the repository unless it is listed below.
#
# Adding a new source file? Add a matching "!name" line, or git will ignore it.
#
# Build artifacts (*.obj, *.exe, *.res, res/*.cur) need no entries of their own:
# the first line already covers them.

*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE
!build.ps1
!extract_cursors.py
!launcher.rc
!resource.h
!Main_min.cpp
!cry_min.h
!CrySystem.def
!docs/
!docs/**.md
